---
term: Voluntary admission
aka:
  - Voluntary association
section: life-cycle
order: 30
definition: The end of the formation gradient at which autonomously organized struggle establishes a charter where it stands, and the charter then seeks [[admission]] into a parent.
seeAlso:
  - charter-formation
  - act-of-commission
  - contract
---
At this end of the gradient, the charter's own members organize it before any parent is involved. The charter then holds a [[contract]] with the parent until admission. The opposite end is an [[act of commission]].
